  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c026", "issues": [
    {"issue": "A holder's access right is qualified by three undefined standards — \"purposes reasonably related to such holder's interests,\" \"does not constitute an undue burden on the Trustee,\" and \"is not detrimental to the Liquidating Trust\" — with no measure and no stated decision-maker. Whether a particular request qualifies cannot be answered from the words used.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c027", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This section lets the Trustee control and dispose of Trust Assets \"without prior or further authorization,\" which cannot be squared with Section 3.3(e), which requires Committee approval for any disposition of an asset worth $5,000 or more. Its opening carve-out refers only to the Trust Agreement and the Plan generally, not to that specific restriction.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
