  {"clause_id": "c028", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This section directs distributions to holders of Class 1 claims, which cannot be squared with the Recitals and Sections 1.1(a) and 2.1, which establish the Trust \"on behalf, and for the benefit, of holders of allowed Class 2 claims\" alone and make Class 2 claimants the only Liquidating Trust Interest holders. Whether Class 1 claimants have any enforceable right against this Trust turns on that conflict.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c029", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The qualifying parenthetical is mispunctuated — \"(including the receipt by the Trustee of a private letter ruling if the Trustee so requests one, or the receipt of an adverse determination by the Internal Revenue Service) upon audit if not contested by the Trustee)\" — with an unmatched closing parenthesis that detaches \"upon audit if not contested.\" It cannot be told whether the audit condition qualifies the adverse determination or the whole grantor-trust filing duty.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.28}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c030", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c031", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This section is numbered \"3.8,\" the same number already used by the immediately preceding \"Reporting by the Trustee\" section, so any cross-reference to Section 3.8 has two possible referents. The duplication is a mechanical numbering error that affects which text a reference picks up.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
    {"issue": "This section speaks of \"proceeds of borrowings, if any,\" but no provision of the instrument grants the Trustee power to borrow — Section 3.2's enumerated powers omit borrowing and Section 4.7(b) merely assumes borrowing \"in accordance with the terms of this Trust Agreement.\" Whether borrowing is authorized at all can only be answered by reading the whole instrument, which does not answer it.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c032", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The exception — \"except that the Trustee may deal with the Trust Assets as permitted by herein\" — is both grammatically incomplete (\"as permitted by herein\") and capable of swallowing the fiduciary-capacity limitation that precedes it. What the Trustee may do outside a fiduciary capacity is left undetermined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c033", "issues": [
    {"issue": "This section imposes an affirmative duty to \"exercise reasonable business judgment in liquidating the Trust Assets,\" which cannot be squared with Section 4.3(a), which exculpates the Trustee from liability for every act or omission short of willful misconduct, gross negligence or fraud. A court would have to decide whether the reasonable-business-judgment duty is enforceable at all.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c034", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The class of exculpated persons shifts inside a single sentence: the protected group is defined as agents or representatives \"of the Trustee,\" but the acts protected are those taken in the capacity of an agent or representative \"of the Liquidating Trust.\" Whether a professional retained by the Trust but not by the Trustee is covered turns on that mismatch.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c035", "issues": [
